{"content":[{"c":["MAMMON*"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Aramaic word, meaning wealth or property, transliterated by the Gospel writers in Greek letters. Some English translations preserve the Greek form of the word in English (",{"c":["kjv"],"sourceClass":"sc","t":"span"},", ",{"c":["rsv"],"sourceClass":"sc","t":"span"},", ",{"c":["nasb"],"sourceClass":"sc","t":"span"},"); others translate it with the words “wealth” or “money” (",{"c":["neb"],"sourceClass":"sc","t":"span"},", ",{"c":["tev"],"sourceClass":"sc","t":"span"},", ",{"c":["niv"],"sourceClass":"sc","t":"span"},", ",{"c":["nlt"],"sourceClass":"sc","t":"span"},"). In ",{"href":"?bref=Matt.6.24","r":"Matt.6.24","rawR":"Matt.6.24","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Matt.6.24","value":"Matt.6.24"}],"t":"ref","v":"Matthew 6:24"}," and ",{"href":"?bref=Luke.16.13","r":"Luke.16.13","rawR":"Luke.16.13","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Luke.16.13","value":"Luke.16.13"}],"t":"ref","v":"Luke 16:13"},", “mammon” is personified as a rival to God for the loyalty of the disciples: To which master will obedience be given? In ",{"href":"?bref=Luke.16.9-11","r":"Luke.16.9-11","rawR":"Luke.16.9-11","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Luke.16.9-11","value":"Luke.16.9-11"}],"t":"ref","v":"Luke 16:9-11"}," the term designates material wealth or property. Mammon itself does not carry a negative value, as the parallel phrasing in ",{"href":"?bref=Luke.16.11","r":"Luke.16.11","rawR":"Luke.16.11","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Luke.16.11","value":"Luke.16.11"}],"t":"ref","v":"Luke 16:11"}," makes clear: “If then you have not been faithful in the unrighteous mammon, who will entrust to you the true riches?” (",{"c":["rsv"],"sourceClass":"sc","t":"span"},")."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Mammon","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Matthew 6:24","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Matt.6.24","rawQueryValue":"Matt.6.24","sourceRefExact":"Matt.6.24"},{"anchorText":"Luke 16:13","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Luke.16.13","rawQueryValue":"Luke.16.13","sourceRefExact":"Luke.16.13"},{"anchorText":"Luke 16:9-11","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Luke.16.9-11","rawQueryValue":"Luke.16.9-11","sourceRefExact":"Luke.16.9-11"},{"anchorText":"Luke 16:11","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Luke.16.11","rawQueryValue":"Luke.16.11","sourceRefExact":"Luke.16.11"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"e0db1a30d046d1c79fe9e99016cd6eb485e75f71b10120217214dae907791181","sourceItemName":"Mammon","sourceItemOrder":103,"sourceMember":"Articles/M.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Mammon","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Mammon*","title":"Mammon*","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}